.policy "ruff-pyi004-patch-version-comparison" revision 2
.description "Compare sys.version_info in a stub file against major and minor versions only; type checkers do not understand patch versions."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PYI004 (flake8-pyi), stubs only: an `if` test comparing sys.version_info (or a slice of it) with a
// tuple of more than two ints. Type checkers read major and minor versions only. The `if` test is checked, or
// each operand of its top-level `and`/`or`, as PYI003 does.
//   if sys.version_info >= (3, 8, 1):    ← PYI004
//   if sys.version_info >= (3, 8):       fine
#include "python/typing.rr"

.violation PYI004(at: node) code "PYI004" "Compare against the major and minor version only, such as `(3, 8)` instead of `(3, 8, 1)`, picking the minor version this branch should cover; type checkers ignore patch versions."
    suppress ruff "PYI004"
PYI004(c) :- stub_test(c), version_cmp(c, f, _, r), f != "other", f != "major", int_tuple(r, k), k > 2.
